MyHumNews — licence terms
=========================

This dataset has two parts under two different sets of rights. Read both.


1. ANNOTATIONS, METADATA, LABEL SCHEMES AND CODE — CC-BY-4.0
------------------------------------------------------------

Copyright (c) 2026 Zwe Htet Aung

The following are the author's own contribution and are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/):

  - the label scheme (dataset/dvb_scheme.py and dataset/outlet_crosswalk.py --
    the merges, the drops, the MIN_SUPPORT cut, and the mapping of four other
    outlets' category vocabularies onto it) and the `topic_dvb19` and
    `topic_dvb19_predicted` fields derived from them
  - the hand-annotated humanitarian gold labels
  - all non-text metadata fields assembled by this project, including the
    deduplication, field normalisation and provenance columns
  - the crawlers, build scripts, evaluation code and documentation

You may share and adapt these for any purpose, including commercially, with
attribution.


2. ARTICLE TEXT — PUBLISHERS' COPYRIGHT, NOT LICENSED BY THE AUTHOR
-------------------------------------------------------------------

The `title` and `body` fields contain the full text of news articles that
remain the copyright of their original publishers:

  - BBC Burmese (British Broadcasting Corporation)
  - DVB (Democratic Voice of Burma)
  - The Irrawaddy
  - Myanmar Now
  - Radio Free Asia (RFA) Burmese

The author does not hold these rights and therefore cannot and does not
license them to you. The CC-BY-4.0 grant in Part 1 does not extend to the
article text.

The text is included for NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH USE. By accessing this
dataset you accept that:

  (a) you will use the article text for non-commercial research only;
  (b) you will not redistribute the article text, in whole or in substantial
      part, whether as a dataset, a derived corpus, or model training data
      made available to others;
  (c) you will not attempt to identify, locate or contact individuals named
      in the articles.

Condition (c) is not a copyright term. Four of the five outlets are exile or
banned Myanmar media, and their reporting names local sources, witnesses and
their families. It is a condition of access regardless of the copyright
position.


3. TAKEDOWN
-----------

Any of the five publishers may request removal of their content, in whole or
in part, with no requirement to give a reason. Such a request will be
honoured, and this dataset will be withdrawn or amended accordingly.

Contact: zwehtetaung.doh@gmail.com

Individuals named in the articles may use the same contact to request removal
of records concerning them.


4. NO WARRANTY
--------------

The dataset is provided as is, without warranty of any kind.

Labels come in two columns and they are not equivalent. Every label in
`topic_dvb19` is a publisher's own category assignment. Every label in
`topic_dvb19_predicted` is the output of a classifier trained on DVB and
applied to all five outlets; measured against other outlets' own labels its
precision ranges from 0.860 down to 0.116, and only two of thirteen testable
labels reach the 0.80 it was tuned for. The two are kept in separate columns so that neither is mistaken
for the other. See the dataset card before using the predicted column for
anything.

The author accepts no liability arising from use of this dataset.
